{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unwhite-thorium-towhee","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Discovered from\n\nCI run 32553346737 on Gerrit change 2065 (ticket d893-e003-0539-47fc): pytest (ubuntu-latest,\npy3.12) failed tests/unit/test_plan_review.py::test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes\nwith 'rebar-version: 0.12.0 (f5fb6e45-dirty)' != 'rebar-version: 0.12.0 (f5fb6e45)' — the -dirty\nsuffix flipped BETWEEN two build_manifest calls inside one test. The same test passes locally.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed by deterministic reproduction)\n\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:497 stamps every manifest with\n`_signing.gate_code_version()`, which shells `git status --porcelain` on the rebar source\ncheckout PER CALL (src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py:_gate_commit_sha). Two byte-equality tests\ncompare manifests built by SEPARATE calls:\n\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review.py:965-966 (test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py:79 (equality of two build_manifest outputs)\n\nUnder pytest-xdist another worker that transiently creates/removes a file in the checkout\n(or any concurrent writer) flips the dirty-state between the calls, so the assertion compares\nracy live-git provenance rather than the file-scope/pins contract under test. Reproduced\ndeterministically: creating a scratch file in the checkout between the two calls makes the\nequality fail with exactly the CI diff.\n\n## Approach\n\nPin the provenance in the affected tests: monkeypatch\n`rebar._signing_manifest.gate_code_version` to a constant in both test functions (manifest.py\nresolves it at call time through the module attribute, so the pin takes effect without touching\nproduction code). The tests then assert the contract they exist for — file-scope back-compat and\npins default-equality — independent of concurrent working-tree state. No production behavior\nchange.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes pins gate_code_version and passes\n      even when a file is created in the checkout between its build_manifest calls — verified by\n      running the test with the reproduction interleaving.\n- [ ] The build_manifest byte-equality in tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py is pinned the\n      same way.\n- [ ] A repo grep shows no remaining test byte-compares two separately-built manifests without\n      pinning gate_code_version.","id":"b44c-2a74-2daf-4b59","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Manifest byte-equality tests sample live git dirty-state and flake under xdist"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787377461405889001,"uuid":"f28b20c8-77e3-4a1e-9833-63dd166def12"}